      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "The app was originally funded by the <b>Kielibuusti</b> project under
    the name <i>CaptainA</i>, its name was changed to <i>SaySuomi</i> during its
    long-term development. When Kielibuusti project ended in 2024, the Aalto ASR
    Research Group responsible for maintaining and further developing the app.\n\nThe
    app uses an idle server from Aalto University. Additional servers for research
    purposes are provided by CSC \u2013 IT Center for Science.\n\nWe especially thank
    the authors of Oma Suomi 1 \u2013 <b>Kristiina Kuparinen</b>, <b>Terhi Tapaninen</b>,
    and <b>Finn Lectura</b> \u2013 for granting us permission to use texts from Oma
    Suomi 1 in the flashcard feature.\n\nWe also thank the authors of Suomen Mestari
    1 \u2013 <b>Sonja Gehring</b>, <b>Sanni Heinzmann</b>, and <b>Finn Lectura</b>
    \u2013 for granting us permission to use texts from Suomen Mestari 1 in the flashcard
    feature.\n\nWe are grateful to<b>Apollo Ailus</b> and <b>Kia Raitanen</b> for
    their contributions to to user research and engagement, and to <b>Aalo Kailu</b>,
    who designed the original user interface of the app.\n\nThe app was created with
    the help of members from the Aalto ASR Research Group.\n\nThe models used in
    this application were trained using computing resources from the Aalto University
    School of Science \"Science-IT\" project.\n\nThe vocabulary learning is based
    on SuperMemo2 algorithm ( https://www.supermemo.com/), with implementation inspired
    by the Anki application (licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License).\n\nIcons
    used in the application are from Google, under the Apache License 2.0.\n\nIllustration
    photos and some video content were created with the assistance of Aija Elg and
    Noora Helki\xF6 from the Aalto University Language Centre.\n\nIllustration pictures
    were provided by Aino Huhtaniemi, used with permission. Some animations were
    modified to include indicators of voiced sounds and tongue movement. Based on
    the work of P\xE4ivi Virkkunen.\n\nImages used in definition of Finnish words
    are created by Midjourney and ChatGPT.\n\nDescriptions of Finnish phoneme and
    their International Phonetic Alphabet (IPA) transcriptions are based on the following
    sources: \"Finnish sound structure: phonetics, phonology, phonotactics and prosody\"
    by  Kari Suomi, Juhani Toivanen & Riikka Ylitalo. \"Fonetiikkaa suomen kielen
    oppijoille\" (Phonetics for Finnish learners) by Eija Aho, Aino Huhtaniemi &
    Mari Nikonen.\n\nMost definitions and etymologies are from Wiktionary.org and
    Sanakirja.org\n\nMost of the audio samples are generated by AI models, including:
    FinSyn TTS by Antti Suni from Helsinki University phonetics group, Narakeet,
    and OpenAI text-to-speech.\n\nAdditional audio samples are from Aalto University
    Language Centre, Common Voice 11.0, licensed under Creative Commons Zero 1.0,
